# Prose is formatted by hand, not by a tool.
#
# This is not a preference. The hygiene gate's waiver comments cover the line
# they sit on and the line after, so a formatter that rewraps a paragraph can
# move a waived line out from under its waiver — turning a documented
# exception into a failure, in a file nobody edited. Reflowing prose also
# makes review harder for no gain: the diff fills with rewrapping.
*.md
docs/

# The hygiene gate and its self-test.
#
# They are pinned by their own tests down to line numbers and exemption lists,
# and they must keep running on a tree with nothing installed. Reformatting
# them is a change to a gate, which is a thing to do deliberately rather than
# as a side effect of running a formatter.
scripts/check-external-refs.mjs
tests/check-external-refs.test.mjs
